{%- doc -%}
  Free shipping status bar, at the very top of the cart.

  Shipping is free on everything except a named set of accessories, and
  even those ship free when they travel with something that qualifies. So
  the test is about what the cart CONTAINS, not what it is worth: one
  qualifying line is enough to unlock the whole order.

  The exclusion list lives in Theme settings → Cart → Free shipping bar and
  is shared with the product page's shipping pill, so the two can't drift.

  No JavaScript: the drawer re-renders from Liquid on every cart update, so
  the bar follows the cart on its own.
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  comment
    Values fall back in Liquid as well as in the schema — a setting that
    exists only as a schema default reads as nil until it reaches
    settings_data.
  endcomment
  assign show_bar = true
  if settings.cart_ship_show == false
    assign show_bar = false
  endif
-%}

{%- capture ship_ok -%}{%- render 'cart-ship-qualified' -%}{%- endcapture -%}

{%- liquid
  assign ship_ok = ship_ok | strip
  assign qualified = false
  if ship_ok == '1'
    assign qualified = true
  endif

  comment
    Nothing to measure, so the fill marks a stage rather than a
    proportion. The bar only renders with something in the cart, so
    reaching it at all means the halfway checkpoint is passed: an
    accessory on its own parks the plane mid-bar, and a qualifying
    product flies it to the end.
  endcomment
  if qualified
    assign pct = 100
  else
    assign pct = 50
  endif

  assign track = settings.cart_ship_track | default: '#e6e6e6'
  assign fill = settings.cart_ship_fill | default: '#16a34a'
  assign fg = settings.cart_ship_text_color | default: '#15803d'
  assign pending_fill = settings.cart_ship_pending_fill | default: '#d1a300'
  assign pending_fg = settings.cart_ship_pending_text_color | default: '#8a6d00'

  assign pending_copy = settings.cart_ship_text_pending | default: 'Add any pair of boots to unlock FREE shipping'
  assign done_copy = settings.cart_ship_text_done | default: 'FREE shipping unlocked'

  if qualified
    assign message = done_copy
  else
    assign message = pending_copy
    assign fill = pending_fill
    assign fg = pending_fg
  endif
-%}

{%- if show_bar and cart.item_count > 0 -%}
  <div
    class="cart-ship{% if qualified %} cart-ship--done{% endif %}"
    style="
      --cs-track: {{ track }};
      --cs-fill: {{ fill }};
      --cs-fg: {{ fg }};
      --cs-pct: {{ pct }}%;
    "
  >
    <p class="cart-ship__text" role="status">
      {%- if qualified -%}
        <span class="cart-ship__tick" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" width="13" height="13">
            <polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/>
          </svg>
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}
      {{ message }}
    </p>

    {%- comment -%}
      The rail sits outside the track because the track clips its fill,
      and the checkpoint and plane both need to overhang it.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="cart-ship__rail">
      <div
        class="cart-ship__track"
        role="progressbar"
        aria-valuemin="0"
        aria-valuemax="100"
        aria-valuenow="{{ pct }}"
        aria-label="{{ message | strip_html | escape }}"
      >
        <span class="cart-ship__fill"></span>
      </div>

      <span class="cart-ship__check{% if pct >= 50 %} cart-ship__check--hit{% endif %}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="cart-ship__plane" aria-hidden="true">&#9992;&#65039;</span>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .cart-ship {
    align-self: stretch;
    width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    margin-block-end: 12px;
  }

  .cart-ship__text {
    margin: 0 0 6px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 5px;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--cs-fg, #15803d);
    font-size: var(--cart-font-size--sm, 0.8rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .cart-ship__tick {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  /* Padded so the plane and the checkpoint, which both stand proud of the
     track, are not clipped by the card above or the list below. */
  .cart-ship__rail {
    position: relative;
    padding-block: 9px;
  }

  .cart-ship__track {
    position: relative;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--cs-track, #e6e6e6);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* Halfway marker. Reached as soon as anything is in the cart, so it is
     the plane's first stop rather than a target to aim at. */
  .cart-ship__check {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    top: 50%;
    width: 9px;
    height: 9px;
    margin: -4.5px 0 0 -4.5px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--cs-track, #e6e6e6);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px rgb(255 255 255 / 85%);
    transition: background-color 0.3s ease;
  }

  .cart-ship__check--hit {
    background: var(--cs-fill, #16a34a);
  }

  /* Rides the head of the fill, at the glyph's own angle. */
  .cart-ship__plane {
    position: absolute;
    left: var(--cs-pct, 0%);
    top: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    font-family: 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Noto Color Emoji', sans-serif;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1;
    filter: drop-shadow(0 1px 2px rgb(0 0 0 / 25%));
    transition: left 0.45s cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.72, 0, 1);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  /* Animated rather than snapped, so adding a qualifying item visibly
     runs the bar to full. The drawer re-renders on cart update, so this
     plays from the previous value each time. */
  .cart-ship__fill {
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    width: var(--cs-pct, 0%);
    border-radius: inherit;
    background: var(--cs-fill, #16a34a);
    transition: width 0.45s cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.72, 0, 1), background-color 0.3s ease;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .cart-ship__fill,
    .cart-ship__plane {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
